    "result_text": "The build succeeds with all tests passing (2/2, 0 failures). Let me confirm the email-domain blocklist still runs before duplicate detection (unchanged ordering in `addOwner`):\n\nThe ordering in `addOwner` (line 208-210) is: `normalizeEmail(...)` \u2014 which throws `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` for blocklisted domains \u2014 runs *before* `rejectDuplicateIdentity(owner)`, so the blocklist is still applied first. \u2713\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key per the specification. All tests pass (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Rewrote `getIdentityKey()` to return the lower-case SHA-256 hex digest over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (was the plain `telephone|email|householdId` triple). `householdId` is no longer part of the key. Added a standard (American) `Soundex` implementation as a `public static` helper (with the H/W adjacency rule) plus a private `sha256Hex` helper.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Updated `applyPossibleDuplicate` so the soft-match now triggers when `soundex(lastName)` **and** `postcode` match but the `identityKey` **differs** (previously: exact last-name match + different telephone). This makes two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones a soft match rather than a hard duplicate. `rejectDuplicateIdentity` is unchanged in behavior \u2014 it remains the single 409 check, still ignoring deleted owners, and the email-domain blocklist still runs first (via `normalizeEmail`, called before it).\n\n3. **Docs** \u2014 Updated the javadoc on `getIdentityKey`, `rejectDuplicateIdentity`, `applyPossibleDuplicate`, the `ExceptionControllerAdvice` handler, and the `identityKey` schema description/example in `openapi.yml` to reflect the new hashed-key definition.\n\nThe separate household-duplicate 409 no longer applies simply because `householdId` was dropped from the identity key \u2014 `applyHousehold` still computes `householdId` for the household member-count and membership-ceiling features, but it no longer participates in duplicate detection.",
